# pico-cam-a-camera

HM01B0 at 324 by 324, 8-bit grayscale over its one-bit serial output.
The SDK adapter owns sensor I2C setup and PIO/DMA capture. It matches the
Waveshare demo's 250 MHz capture clock (above the rated 200 MHz point),
using 1.15 V, and waits 10 ms after each initialization register write.
The fixed oscillator supplies MCLK; no GPIO clock or reset is driven. Capture waits for a fresh
FVLD edge and gives both frame synchronization and DMA one shared deadline.
